# Allowlist ONLY these hosts. One host per line, matched as an FQDN
# (see tinyproxy.conf: FilterExtended On).
# 1. The upstream Metro Train GTFS-Realtime gateway.
^api\.opendata\.transport\.vic\.gov\.au$
# 2. The external dead-man's-switch ping target — deliberate, narrow
# widening, not the default upstream host.
^hc-ping\.com$
# 3. The static GTFS schedule portal — deliberately the PLAIN host, not the
# `api.` gateway above: this is a different, unauthenticated CKAN endpoint
# on the same parent domain, not a redirect target.
^opendata\.transport\.vic\.gov\.au$
# 4. Anthropic API — Haiku calls from ai/llm_client.py.
^api\.anthropic\.com$
# 5. Langfuse Cloud — matches the actual configured LANGFUSE_BASE_URL
# value, not assumed.
^cloud\.langfuse\.com$
# 6. Slack incoming webhooks — fixed host regardless of which
# webhook/workspace/channel TT_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL actually points at (also
# used by the poller directly, not just Grafana — see docker-compose.yml).
^hooks\.slack\.com$
# 7. Flagsmith remote-evaluation API (feature-toggle system) — SaaS default
# host; only the api service's process calls this (flags/client.py), not
# the poller.
^edge\.api\.flagsmith\.com$
# 8. Hugging Face archive pipeline — huggingface_hub's real upload path
# hits TWO hosts, not one: the main API, and a separate "xet" storage/CDN
# backend that actually carries the file bytes. A single-hostname filter
# would silently break real uploads. Only the archiver service calls these,
# not the poller.
^huggingface\.co$
^cas-server\.xethub\.hf\.co$
